  "notes": [
    "The gate below was registered at pending in an earlier commit, before anything ran, and is unchanged. protocolDigest covers it, so loosening it after seeing the numbers would show up in the diff as a changed protocol rather than as one moved number. The result did not meet it and the record says so.",
    "The disagreement is one-directional and concentrated. Of the 9813 returns the two sides labelled differently across the five scenes, 9812 are bare earth as the scene was built and 9810 are returns only the reference called ground; the two agree completely about every building and vegetation return in every scene. The planar scenes agree exactly, and the three that do not are the ones carrying curvature, a 30 % gradient, or gross low returns. Where that difference comes from is not settled by this study and is not asserted here.",
    "This record promotes nothing. docs/validation/claim-register.yaml and REFERENCE_SLOTS in src/validation/crossCheck.ts are untouched, and promotion is a separate human act.",
    "The comparison is our SMRF against PDAL's filters.smrf on the same committed bytes, with cut disabled on the PDAL side and the threshold cap disabled on ours, so the two sides run the same published core with the same parameters."
